      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{wy+6y}{{w}^{2}+2w-24}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The numerator can be factored as $wy+6y=y(w+6)$ and the denominator can be factored as ${w}^{2}+2w-24=(w+6)(w-4).$ Canceling out any common factors that appear in the numerator and the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{wy+6y}{{w}^{2}+2w-24} & =\\frac{y(w+6)}{(w+6)(w-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\cancel{(w+6)}}{\\cancel{(w+6)}(w-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{w-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
